# The SDD record is tracked deliberately: the per-task briefs, the implementer
# reports, the review packages, and the test-evidence logs are the evidence
# behind each task's verdict and each ruling in the ledgers.
#
# This file IS tracked -- the `!.gitignore` arm below is what lets that happen,
# and it has to be: it is the rule that makes the record visible, and a rule that
# lived in one working tree would be lost by the next clone.
#
# `*` keeps a NEW phase invisible until someone decides otherwise; each pair of
# negations below is that decision for one phase, and a phase is added by
# negating its directory and then its contents, in that order. `tools/sdd/
# sdd-workspace.ps1` creates this file when it is missing and never rewrites it,
# because a run that overwrote it would silently hide every phase at once.
*
!.gitignore
!2026-09-25-turing-complete-phase0/
!2026-09-25-turing-complete-phase0/**
!2026-09-25-turing-complete-phase1/
!2026-09-25-turing-complete-phase1/**
!2026-09-29-turing-complete-phase2/
!2026-09-29-turing-complete-phase2/**
!2026-10-04-turing-complete-2x-realign/
!2026-10-04-turing-complete-2x-realign/**
!2026-10-08-turing-complete-phase3/
!2026-10-08-turing-complete-phase3/**
